MENTOR: You're right. The curve is a hill with its peak in the middle, and that's what Easy Ease gives you.

I rendered the frame at 1 s, halfway through that move. It came back as a plain purple field, so I can't make out where Title is. The graph will tell us more anyway.

**How the speed graph works:** each key has a handle that sticks out sideways. How far it reaches is the **influence**, which is how long the ease lasts. Easy Ease gives every key the same reach, so every move has the same middle-peak feel.

- **Short reach out of the key at 0.5 s:** Title gets up to speed quickly, so the move starts snappy.
- **Long reach into the key at 1.5 s:** Title slows down over more of the move, so it lands softly.

Keep the landing handle **on the bottom** of the graph. If you drag it up, Title arrives still moving. Drag it sideways only, to make it longer or shorter.

You could also type the influence in the Keyframe Velocity dialog instead of dragging, if you prefer.

Try it on Title's Position from 0.5 to 1.5 s: a short ease out, a long ease in. Do the same for the other two Position moves and for Scale, then say "done".
